;; Reading sets: the named path lists a cold session of a given task class reads
;; before starting work, plus a `:budget-lines` integer per set.
;; `ehrt.docs-tooling.reading-set-budget-test` resolves every path (a ghost is
;; red), sums real line counts, and fails any set over its own budget.
;;
;; Composition principle (AR-1): prefer omission. A path here is a path every
;; future session of that class reads cold, forever.
;;
;; THE RATCHET (ADR-0143 guard #3): a budget may never EXCEED its entry in
;; `.agents/reading-sets-baseline.edn`, and may always fall. Over budget, a
;; session compacts or STOPs -- it does not bump (`rulings.md#R-budget-stop`).
;; Only a compaction ADR moves a baseline, using the standing formula: that
;; ADR's own post-compaction measured actual x 1.15, rounded up to the nearest 5.
;;
;; This header is capped at 20 comment lines (ADR-0145). Everything it replaced
;; -- the seed note, the migration-session notes, nineteen dated budget
;; re-derivations 2026-08-05 to 2026-08-17, and the per-set composition
;; rationale that used to sit inside the map -- is VERBATIM in
;; `.agents/plans/reading-sets-history.md`. Read that before editing a set.

